@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' Destination diagram — prose from internal/choiceui/choiceui.go and cmd/proveo/main.go's
' row-gating helpers (applicableRows, comingSoon, gateAddons, gateEvidence) lands here (batches 3 and 6).
' What the answers MEAN and how they are cached: _spec/internal/agentsettings/choice-cache.puml.
' Resolved geometry — column alignment, the divider, how a gated element is drawn:
' _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml (salt). Layout prose belongs there, not here.
' Why review needs a pty: _spec/internal/reviewgate/pty-review-proxy.puml.
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
title Choice prompt render — radio axes above the divider, checkboxes below

node "internal/choiceui" as PKG <<host>> {
  component "Form\nBanner · Title · Header · Rows" as FORM <<app>>
  component "Row\nradio: Options + Selected\ncheckbox: Multi + On/Off" as ROW <<app>>
  component "draw(screen, cursor)\nlegend · divider · markers" as DRAW <<app>>
  component "Run()\ntcell screen, one key per action" as RUN <<app>>
  component "OnChange(*Form)\nre-gated after every keystroke" as CHANGE <<app>>
  component "Selection · Selections\nread back by label" as READ <<app>>
}

node "cmd/proveo — what may be offered" as GATES <<host>> {
  component "applicableRows\ndrop an axis with nothing to decide" as APPL <<app>>
  component "comingSoon\ngrey out + move the selection off" as SOON <<app>>
  component "gateAddons · gateEvidence\ncross-row exclusivity" as GATE <<app>>
}

component "Operator terminal\nrequires a TTY" as TTY <<host>>
component "EnvHeader\ndetected secrets · settings" as HDR <<app>>
component "A locked or absent row read as an answer" as MISREAD <<error>>

GATES ARROW_MAIN FORM : rows built, then filtered
HDR ARROW_MAIN FORM
FORM ARROW_MAIN ROW
FORM ARROW_MAIN DRAW
RUN ARROW_MAIN DRAW : redraw per event
RUN ARROW_MAIN CHANGE
CHANGE ARROW_MAIN GATE
APPL ARROW_MAIN FORM
SOON ARROW_MAIN ROW
DRAW ARROW_MAIN TTY
TTY ARROW_MAIN RUN : Enter confirms · Esc/q cancels
RUN ARROW_MAIN READ
READ ARROW_ERROR MISREAD : fall back to the resolved value instead

note bottom of DRAW
  **""agent evidence"" is a toggle, not a tier.**
  Narrating more of the run costs tokens and
  screen rather than safety, so it belongs with
  the add-ons instead of under the legend, and
  ""gateEvidence"" enforces their exclusivity.
end note

note bottom of DRAW
  **Ordering is a property of the row, not of
  the prompt.** The radio axes run riskier →
  safer while a checkbox set carries no such
  direction, so a single legend cannot describe
  both and the divider ends its authority.
end note

note top of GATE
  **One gate per toggle row, run
  unconditionally.** ""gateAddons"" degrades to a
  no-op when its row was filtered out, so both
  gates fire on every keystroke and the caller
  never tracks which rows survived onto the form.
end note

note top of GATE
  **A level is one answer.** ""gateEvidence""
  clears the opposite box whenever either is
  ticked, and clearing both is allowed because
  ""evidenceFrom"" only asks whether verbose was
  selected.
end note

note top of SOON
  **Greyed, never hidden.** ""comingSoon""
  disables the option and moves the selection
  away, yet the row still displays it with the
  reason attached, because removing it
  misrepresents an unfinished tier as absent.
end note

note bottom of SOON
  **""--egress-mode"" still accepts the value.**
  Development can therefore drive an unfinished
  tier that an operator cannot select by
  accident, and ""review"" is greyed by its
  platform with the failed constraint named.
end note

note top of TTY
  **""isStdinTTY"" gates every interactive
  prompt.** It performs a genuine ioctl check
  rather than a character-device stat, because
  ""/dev/null"" is itself a character device and
  would block a run that can never reply.
end note

note bottom of TTY
  **The add-ons picker runs BEFORE the
  missing-env wizard.** The wizard may attach a
  ""bufio\.Reader"" to stdin, and a buffered
  reader starves the picker of the keystrokes it
  is waiting for, hanging the prompt entirely.
end note

note top of HDR
  **Models are shown, not chosen.** The grid
  holds closed choices while a model id is an
  unbounded value, so the roles are printed in
  the header beside the repository instead of
  becoming a selectable row of their own.
end note

note bottom of HDR
  **Each role carries the provider it resolved
  to.** That is what exposes a credential-less
  role BEFORE launch, rather than after an
  authentication failure on its first outbound
  call.
end note

note bottom of ROW
  Checkboxes render under
  an add-ons divider.
end note

note bottom of ROW
  **The consent modal takes the whole screen.**
  ""review"" mode answers one connection at a time
  over a suspended agent TUI.
end note


@enduml
